WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.600 --> 00:00:10.794
Hi! Today we'll work backwards: use the area or perimeter to find a missing side. We'll also try composite figures.

2
00:00:10.944 --> 00:00:16.746
Area is length times breadth. So the breadth is the area divided by the length.

3
00:00:16.896 --> 00:00:26.298
If the area is 48 square centimetres and the length is 8 cm, the breadth is 48 divided by 8, which is 6 cm.

4
00:00:26.448 --> 00:00:40.554
A perimeter is two lengths plus two breadths. If it is 30 cm, half of it, 15, is one length plus one breadth. 15 minus 9 gives a breadth of 6 cm.

5
00:00:40.704 --> 00:00:52.674
A square has four equal sides. If its area is 49 square centimetres, which number times itself is 49? It's 7, so the side is 7 cm.

6
00:00:52.824 --> 00:01:00.930
If the perimeter is 36 cm, divide by 4. Each side is 9 cm.

7
00:01:01.080 --> 00:01:05.994
Now look at this composite figure. It is made up of rectangles.

8
00:01:06.144 --> 00:01:12.882
Split it into two rectangles: 10 times 5 is 50, and 6 times 3 is 18.

9
00:01:13.032 --> 00:01:17.562
Add them up: the area is 68 square centimetres.

10
00:01:17.712 --> 00:01:28.218
For the perimeter, add all six sides round the outside: 10, 5, 4, 3, 6 and 8 make 36 cm.

11
00:01:28.368 --> 00:01:34.530
Watch out! Finding the breadth by doing 30 minus 9 to get 21 is wrong!

12
00:01:34.680 --> 00:01:40.962
Divide the perimeter by 2 first to get one length plus one breadth, then subtract the length.

13
00:01:41.112 --> 00:01:47.754
Check: 9 plus 6 plus 9 plus 6 is exactly 30.

14
00:01:47.904 --> 00:02:01.026
Your turn! A rectangle has an area of 72 square centimetres and a breadth of 6 cm. What is its length? Pause and think.

15
00:02:01.176 --> 00:02:09.210
72 divided by 6 is 12, so the length is 12 cm. Did you get it right?

16
00:02:09.360 --> 00:02:20.394
Another one! A square has a perimeter of 28 cm. What is its area? Pause and think.

17
00:02:20.544 --> 00:02:32.658
Each side is 28 divided by 4, which is 7 cm. The area is 7 times 7, which is 49 square centimetres. Did you get it right?

18
00:02:32.808 --> 00:02:45.522
Last one! A rectangle has a perimeter of 40 cm and a length of 12 cm. What is its breadth? Pause and think.

19
00:02:45.672 --> 00:02:55.314
40 divided by 2 is 20, and 20 minus 12 is 8. The breadth is 8 cm. Did you get it right?

20
00:02:55.464 --> 00:03:02.706
Remember: divide the area by one side to find the other. From a perimeter, halve it, then subtract.

21
00:03:02.856 --> 00:03:14.346
For a square, find the number that times itself gives the area, or divide the perimeter by 4. For composite figures, split them for area, and go round the outside for perimeter.

22
00:03:14.496 --> 00:03:19.674
Next time, measure your desk and work out its area!

